course: dictionary
lesson: 5817
title: Magnify: making things look bigger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To magnify something means to make it look bigger than it really is. A magnifying glass does this with a curved lens. «Hold a magnifying glass over an ant and the bent light makes the ant look huge.» The ant is not really bigger. It only looks bigger through the lens.
explain: Magnify has a second meaning too: to make a problem seem bigger or worse than it really is. If someone says «don't magnify the problem», they mean don't make a small thing sound like a big thing.
explain: Scientists use a magnifying glass to look at minibeasts, leaves and crystals. A microscope magnifies things far more, so tiny cells become visible. Never look at the Sun through a lens, because the lens can gather sunlight into a tiny spot that is hot enough to start a fire.
fact: «Magnify» means to make something look bigger than it really is, using a lens or microscope.
fact: A magnifying glass is thicker in the middle and bends light inwards, which makes small things look bigger.
fact: «Magnified ×10» means the thing looks ten times bigger in length.
fact: A microscope magnifies cells many times, so tiny parts of living things can be seen.
fact: Magnify can also mean to make a problem seem bigger or worse than it really is, as in «magnify a problem».
fact: Never point a magnifying glass at the Sun, because the lens can start a fire.
exercise: A scientist uses a hand lens to look at a leaf. What does magnify mean here? | Make the leaf change colour | *Make the leaf look bigger than it really is | Cut the leaf into smaller pieces | Make the leaf heavier
exercise: Why should you never look at the Sun through a magnifying glass? | The glass turns green in the light | *The lens can gather sunlight into a spot hot enough to start a fire | It makes the Sun look smaller | The Sun is too far away to see
exercise: Mum says, «Don't magnify the problem, it's only a small spill.» What does magnify mean? | *To make the problem seem bigger than it really is | To clean up the problem quickly | To make the problem disappear | To make the problem louder
test: In «magnified ×10», how much bigger does the thing look? | *Ten times bigger in length | Exactly the same size | Ten times lighter | Ten years older
test: What shape is a magnifying glass lens? | Thin in the middle and thick at the edges | Flat all the way across | *Thicker in the middle, bending light inwards | Square with sharp corners
exam: Which sentence uses magnify to mean making something seem worse than it really is? | *Dad said, «Don't magnify the problem, it's only a scratch.» | The lens magnifies the ant | The Sun is magnified by the glass | The microscope magnifies the cells
